fectively.", "ZARAZAGA ET AL:Zarazaga et al is a reference to a group of researchers who conducted a review on dietary recommendations for patients with chronic kidney disease.", "KIDNEY FOUNDATION:The Kidney Foundation provides guidelines and recommendations for the nutritional management of patients with kidney disease.", "DIALYSIS PERITONEAL:DIALYSIS PERITONEAL refers to peritoneal dialysis, a treatment for kidney failure that utilizes the lining of the abdomen to filter waste from the blood. This method effectively removes toxins and excess fluids, providing an alternative to traditional hemodialysis for patients with compromised kidney function.", "NUTRICIÓN EN LA INSUFICIENCIA RENAL CRÓNICA:Nutritional management in chronic kidney disease focuses on maintaining nutritional status and improving quality of life for patients.", "ACIDOSIS:Acidosis is a metabolic condition that can significantly impact patients with chronic kidney disease, influencing their nutritional status and treatment options. Additionally, it is a chronic state that affects individuals following a ketogenic diet, increasing the risk of bone demineralization. This dual impact highlights the importance of monitoring and managing acidosis in both chronic kidney disease patients and those adhering to specific dietary regimens.", "INSULINORRESISTENCIA:Insulin resistance is a condition characterized by the body's cells failing to respond effectively to insulin. This condition can complicate the management of patients with chronic kidney disease, as it impacts their nutritional needs. Additionally, insulin resistance may be exacerbated by surgical stress, further complicating the overall health and treatment of affected individuals.", "SUPLEMENTOS DIETÉTICOS:Dietary supplements are used to ensure adequate nutrient intake in patients with chronic kidney disease, particularly those with protein restrictions.", "NUTRICIÓN EN PREDIALISIS:Nutrition in pre-dialysis focuses on maintaining nutritional status before the initiation of dialysis treatment in patients with chronic kidney disease.", "NUTRICIÓN EN HEMODIÁLISIS:Nutrition in hemodialysis involves specific dietary recommendations to support patients undergoing this treatment for kidney failure.", "NUTRICIÓN EN DIÁLISIS PERITONEAL:Nutrition in peritoneal dialysis addresses the unique dietary needs of patients receiving this form of kidney treatment.", "NEFROPATÍA:Nefropatía refers to kidney disease, which can be managed with dietary adjustments and nutritional support.", "DIETA BAJA EN PROTEÍNAS:A low-protein diet is recommended for patients with renal insufficiency to manage their condition.", "RADICALES LIBRES:Free radicals are harmful compounds that can be produced in excess due to renal dysfunction, and dietary management aims to reduce their production."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}